    description: "WHAT, after PR #2200:\n- `func (s *Stack[T]) Push` is named `Push`, not `Stack.Push`.\n- Grouped parameters (`a, b int`) hash the first name; tuple-result elements hash their names (MOVES IDS if fixed).\n- The pointer strip on receivers is deliberate (commit 23708dff23) and was kept.\n- Symbol.signature does not show type parameters.\n\nFixing a part marked MOVES IDS changes hashed input, so it belongs to the next stable-id bump, with a measured churn figure in the spec's history row.\n\nFound during PR 2 of the stable-id plan (the v15 bump), 2026-11-16 (PR #2200). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/STATUS.md."  # 60b6
